{
	title: 'Settings: config.ason over local.ts',
	description: "Two layers. config.ason in the home root (next to the credentials file; user-edited, like a dotfile) holds the common settings, and only those declared in one table in src/common/settings.ts: name, type, default, one-line description. That table validates the file, documents it, and is what /config renders (each type maps to a form field, tasks/w4/forms.md). The file is a live file: edits apply at once, code reads settings.<name>() at call time. A missing file means all defaults; an unknown key or bad value is a visible warning and that setting falls back to its default, never silently ignored and never a crash. local.ts stays the unlimited escape hatch: it runs after config and may replace any exported function, settings.* included. First settings: model (default model), security (best-effort | none, tasks/6f), web password and port. Replace the README rule 'No config file' with this.",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: [],
	foldInto: ['9']
}
